WEBVTT

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:36.490
Those are...

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:38.620
Space battleships of Neo Atlantis!

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.200
What do you mean?

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:41.370
Evil ships!

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:43.330
Let's take cover quickly!

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:44.950
Gotcha!

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:49.210
Wait up!

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:57.550
This isn't good.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.590
I never imagined they'd come all the way here.

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:00.890
Why did they come here?

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:03.510
Are they here to find Nadia?

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:04.350
Impossible!

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:06.480
No, it's very possible.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.600
Did they see us?

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:20.660
Ship number two, the Deus Ex Machina

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:22.370
has sent a message saying they've discovered Nadia.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:24.620
What? Nadia?

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:26.540
Is she alive?

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:28.080
Stop babbling!

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:34.800
Even Emperor Neo couldn't find the Blue Water yet. This means

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:38.630
Nadia and Nemo could both still be alive.

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:39.550
Sir!

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:44.310
We've returned to the ruins of Tartessos after so long a time.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:46.810
This is a lucky thing to find.

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.890
This is a terrible thing to find!

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:50.060
What'll we do?

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:54.400
Run away, of course! Those monsters sank the Nautilus!

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.150
The best way is to run away.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:58.900
Okay, let's...

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:00.910
Nice to see you again, Nadia.

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:02.870
Gargoyle!

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:04.580
Who is he?

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:05.870
The bad guy!

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:10.080
Now, Nadia, come out with your Blue Water.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.540
You can save your friends' lives that way.

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:16.750
You don't have to go!

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:20.090
Right, they'll try to kill us anyway.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.300
It seems you can't decide.

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:28.060
I will show you what will happen to you if you don't.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:34.360
That's...

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:39.820
Damn!

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:53.460
Nadia, I will give you sixty seconds.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:57.340
You must bid farewell to your friends.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:58.920
Ignore him!

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:01.630
But we'll all be killed soon.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:05.260
I don't want to die here without knowing anything.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.430
You mean you want her to go?

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.890
Yes, that's the best way.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:13.850
You keep your mouth shut!

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:14.600
I'm going!

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.480
Ayerton is right.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:22.700
We'll all be killed otherwise.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.490
We'll end up like that!

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.700
But...

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:32.500
Nadia, I promise I'll rescue you!

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.420
I'll be waiting.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:15.290
Here I am! If you promise me you'll spare them,

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:18.000
I'll give you the Blue Water!

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.210
Okay, I promise.

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:24.970
Nadia!

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:29.050
Don't worry, Marie.

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:31.470
I have the power to destroy the world.

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:33.180
They'll never beat me.

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:34.270
But...

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:38.860
Don't worry! I'm sure Jean will come to rescue me.

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:42.780
Be a good girl. I'll be back soon.

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:44.990
Okay, I'll wait!

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:47.200
Good girl.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:53.410
Nadia!

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:07.090
Lord Gargoyle, we have picked up Princess Nadia.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:11.260
Right. Bring her here, but be courteous.

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:12.470
Yes, Sir!

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:16.890
Now, I will give them a chance.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:17.980
What'll we do?

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:22.150
Let's run to the Gratan as fast as we can!

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:24.360
And figure it out later?

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:26.740
Well, my friends!

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:31.070
You have a chance to survive now.

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:36.040
I'll give you one minute. You can flee anywhere you like.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:38.290
Damn, how cruel he is!

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:40.080
We don't have time! Let's leave quickly!

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:44.210
Gotcha! You'll be sorry someday, Gargoyle!

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:48.760
My friends, you have just forty seconds left.

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:49.880
Villain!

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:59.270
Don't be so rude to our guest.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:06.320
Well, well, Princess Nadia,

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:10.320
I am honored to be able to see you again.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:12.820
You liar! You said you would spare them!

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:15.330
You are accusing me falsely, Nadia.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:20.920
I gave them a chance to survive. That's enough.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:26.380
All of you would have been dead if you hadn't come out.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:29.880
You should be thankful to me.

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:31.800
You're not human!

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:38.470
Of course not! I told you not to confuse me with those foolish creatures.

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:40.810
It is time now, Lord Gargoyle.

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:45.440
Open fire! Aim three hundred meters away at first.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:48.030
Move it closer by fifty meters each time after that.

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:56.830
Do you see, Nadia? I'm quite merciful, am I not?

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:01.330
They have another chance to survive now.

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:07.250
Damn, they'll get us sooner or later!

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:09.760
The explosions are getting closer!

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:12.340
They're trying to kill us an inch at a time!

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:20.680
Damn! Can't you find the Gratan yet?

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:29.440
The Gratan!

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:30.570
Lucky!

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:32.900
There's nothing to be afraid of once we're in this!

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:39.830
The target is moving faster.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:43.290
It seems they're in a vehicle now.

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:49.050
Can't you speed this thing up?

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:50.920
This is as fast as it goes!

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:54.050
It's gotten pretty damaged.

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:58.930
There it is again!

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:00.720
So persistent!

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:07.020
Oh, boy. I don't think the roof will last long.

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:09.770
Let's get out of here quickly!

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:17.320
It's moving too fast now!

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:21.040
Yeah, too much speed will cause an accident.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:24.120
Shut up! The brakes are out of order!

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:27.370
I can't stop it!

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:30.750
Put the gears in reverse!

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:33.260
No, the gears would blow!

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:34.470
The cylinder!

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:36.630
Good idea!

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:44.060
We're still going down!

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:47.390
I'm afraid this thing will hit a wall!

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:49.560
This will sure be the end of us.

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:53.280
The exit!

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:55.990
Lucky!

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:00.700
Not lucky!

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:04.410
No balloon!

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:07.120
You've got to do something!

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:08.790
That's right, the cylinder!

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:09.630
Yeah!

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:14.590
It won't reach!

00:10:14.590 --> 00:10:15.880
What the hell?

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:17.800
This is too high to be safe.

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:23.390
And the graveyard is under us.

00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:25.560
That'll be a timesaver.

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:27.520
It was a brief life.

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:32.190
I'm bored.

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:36.360
What's the matter?

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:37.950
Have we crashed already?

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:39.910
No, we're in the air!

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:47.580
What's that?

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:48.790
We're safe!

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:55.590
The target has come into contact with something.

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:58.340
It's finally trapped.

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:01.550
Yes, they've snapped at the bait now.

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:05.560
Where are they taking us?

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:08.930
We can't do anything regardless.

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:10.390
Yes, indeed.

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:12.690
We've stopped.

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:14.440
Yeah, we've reached the ground

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:16.400
That ship is coming down too.

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:20.530
Right!

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:22.240
Sanson!

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:24.120
I know.

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:30.870
That thing...

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:34.540
What a strangely shaped airplane.

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:38.210
How could it fly without wings?

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:40.300
Just like the ship we saw before.

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:41.880
You mean from Neo Atlantis?

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:44.550
It wouldn't have helped us if it was.

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:46.430
It would have.

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:49.270
Yeah, they might be thinking of wrapping up this affair here.

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:52.480
I don't like that ship!

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:05.570
Miss Electra!

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:14.630
Nice to see you again.

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:17.840
What, you're safe!

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:20.260
Yes, you all saved my life.

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:23.430
I thank you so much for that.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:26.510
Is everyone okay?

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:29.270
They took Nadia away!

00:12:29.270 --> 00:12:32.730
Yes, I know. I'm sorry I couldn't get there in time.

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:33.850
Will you help her now?

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:36.690
It's not the right time now.

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:39.150
We should wait for a good chance.

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:45.910
I'll talk to you later, just follow me for now.

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:47.870
Captain Nemo is waiting for you.

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:49.790
Captain Nemo?

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:52.790
Yes, he must be alive.

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:57.000
We've detected a high energy reaction underground here.

00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:00.500
It seems that one of the ruins is still alive.

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:05.050
The only ones who know the secret of this place are Nemo and us.

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:09.560
That means Nemo is still alive here.

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:13.060
The target is going into the sixth area.

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:20.520
Captain Nemo, I knew I'd be able to see you again someday,

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:23.150
but I didn't imagine it would be today!

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:26.030
I knew this would happen.

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:26.660
Really!

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:31.660
Captain Nemo...

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:41.550
The target's reaction just disappeared in the seventh area.

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:44.630
The wave is probably being screened by something.

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:49.300
Nemo must be hiding there. Get ready to attack!

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:51.600
Yes, Sir! Ready the guns!

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:55.140
Did you do this to find out where Captain Nemo was?

00:13:55.140 --> 00:14:00.020
Exactly. Did you believe I would let such useless people live?

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:01.690
Foolish girl.

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:12.910
What a long tunnel.

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:16.410
How far are we going?

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:17.120
Here we are.

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:18.040
Here?

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:25.960
That funny building?

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:27.970
No, that's a ship.

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:29.220
A ship?

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:32.930
What the heck are you talking about? We're underground here!

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:35.520
A ship should be floating on water!

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:37.640
You'll understand soon enough.

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:47.030
This elevator tilts as it's going up.

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:52.070
You've arrived?

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:54.620
Captain Nemo!

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:56.290
Where are...

00:14:56.870 --> 00:14:58.870
The first bridge.

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:00.420
The first bridge?

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:03.250
You mean this is a ship?

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:04.590
That's right.

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:06.260
You are...

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:07.460
Miss Ikorina!

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:08.590
Yo!

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:11.430
Everyone's here!

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:13.100
You're all safe!

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:14.850
How were you able to...

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:17.060
Let's talk about it later.

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:20.060
There are two flies buzzing about us now.

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:24.690
Captain, we've got the space battleships on screen.

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:26.570
Right, put it on the main screen.

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:28.110
Aye, aye!

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:32.700
Gargoyle has noticed us.

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:41.370
Damn, they've started firing!

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:57.430
Damn, we'll be blasted to bits soon!

00:15:57.430 --> 00:15:59.770
Is this ship unable to move?

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:01.770
Captain Nemo!

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:10.610
How is the auxiliary particle annihilation engine?

00:16:10.610 --> 00:16:12.400
No good! It doesn't work yet!

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:17.830
This ship means nothing if the engine doesn't work.

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:21.620
Their energy readings are still in good condition.

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:24.290
This is taking too long.

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:26.000
Fire the full sized annihilation bomb.

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:26.590
Yes, Sir!

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:39.930
We did it!

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:43.020
They can't survive this time.

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:47.020
It seems we're still alive.

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:49.190
We thought we were dead!

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:51.030
But it's so dark!

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:54.860
Are we going to live in this darkness forever?

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:56.820
Switching to backup power.

00:16:58.490 --> 00:17:00.410
We're buried alive!

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:03.750
That was really a huge bomb.

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:05.920
We were lucky we could survive.

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:09.040
Fire one more to make sure.

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:11.380
Yes, Sir! Hurry up and reload!

00:17:16.340 --> 00:17:18.550
Oh, man! They're trying to give us the finishing blow!

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:20.430
Is this ship still unable to fight?

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:21.060
Captain!

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:23.930
The auxiliary particle annihilation engine checks out!

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:26.230
The flywheel joint is ready!

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:33.650
Start the auxiliary particle annihilation engine.

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:35.700
Prepare the electron turrets.

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:38.280
Readying the electron turrets.

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:45.330
Prepare for launch. Right the ship!

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:46.540
Righting the ship!

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:48.290
Anti-gravity screw, contact.

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:52.500
Raise thrust to 11,600,000 tons! Let's go!

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:54.630
Launch, New Nautilus!

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:57.090
New Nautilus? This thing?

00:17:57.090 --> 00:18:00.930
Yes, this is the battleship, New Nautilus!

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:03.810
This, from those miserable ruins?

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:12.070
Yes, it is born again.

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:26.040
That's...

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:27.290
What's going on?

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:30.250
Impossible, the elusive sunken battleship?

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:35.840
Scanning with the main radar!

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:38.090
Generator power at one hundred percent.

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:40.970
All cylinders, pressure is normal.

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:43.760
The targets are the space battleships.

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:45.770
First turret, fire at will!

00:18:45.770 --> 00:18:48.310
Targeting the space battleships.

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:50.350
Transferring power to the first turret.

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:58.570
Their main turret is rotating.

00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:00.780
What? Fire quickly!

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:09.040
A barrier?

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:10.120
That's right.

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.540
The target has been picked up on radar.

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:14.630
The homing device is ready to charge.

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:20.180
Pressure within limits.

00:19:20.180 --> 00:19:21.640
Charging of gunpowder is complete.

00:19:23.510 --> 00:19:25.060
Target distance computed.

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:28.270
Error correction, one degree right, three degrees vertical.

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:29.850
Ready to fire.

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:31.020
Fire!

00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:32.230
Firing!

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:43.700
All right!

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:54.040
The Deus Ex Machina was destroyed with a single blow!

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:55.210
I can't believe it!

00:19:56.670 --> 00:19:58.000
That power...

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:02.510
They must have revived the legendary annihilation weapon, Excelion.

00:20:07.430 --> 00:20:09.890
We've been locked onto by one of their turrets!

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:11.390
What?

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:14.980
Lord Gargoyle, they're trying to hail us.

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:15.730
Put it through.

00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:16.270
Yes, Sir!

00:20:17.940 --> 00:20:19.610
It's been a long time, Gargoyle.

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:23.740
I thought I'd never talk to you like this again, Nemo.

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:25.780
I'd never have dreamed it.

00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:28.120
I'm sorry. By the way...

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:32.500
I want my daughter back. I know she is on your ship.

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:36.040
I'm sorry, but I can't do that.

00:20:37.590 --> 00:20:40.590
In that case, I must use my power.

00:20:40.590 --> 00:20:46.090
I don't think you can do it. You can't kill your daughter.

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:52.930
Now, Nemo, give me your Blue Water if you wish your daughter to live for long.

00:20:52.930 --> 00:20:54.390
Blue Water!

00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:56.940
You have a Blue Water too, Captain Nemo?

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:00.900
So, what will you do, Nemo?

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:02.610
I won't!

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:03.740
Captain Nemo!

00:21:04.110 --> 00:21:06.160
Fire the main turret, First Officer!

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:06.820
But...

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:08.160
Go on! Fire!

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:11.240
Aye.

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:21.800
I promised Nadia that I'd rescue her for sure.

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:23.920
Jean...

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:29.050
But we must settle this before Nadia is used by Gargoyle.

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:31.720
Captain, you should think about one life

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:34.480
before you think about many lives!

00:21:35.730 --> 00:21:37.520
Captain!

00:21:37.810 --> 00:21:40.150
Please, Captain Nemo!

00:21:49.450 --> 00:21:52.370
Gargoyle, here is my Blue Water.

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:54.000
Why don't you come and get it?

00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:55.330
Captain!

00:21:58.500 --> 00:22:01.710
I don't have to do that.

00:22:08.430 --> 00:22:10.010
What's happening?

00:22:14.560 --> 00:22:16.020
It's gone!

00:22:16.230 --> 00:22:17.480
The Blue Water!

00:22:17.730 --> 00:22:21.230
Impossible! Is it Neo? Is he there?

00:22:21.820 --> 00:22:26.900
That's right. Emperor Neo is here on this occasion.

00:22:26.900 --> 00:22:30.870
But Emperor Neo's power is not that strong!

00:22:33.910 --> 00:22:37.870
Are you surprised at the Emperor's power?

00:22:37.870 --> 00:22:40.670
He's not a child anymore.

00:22:40.670 --> 00:22:45.760
And we have excellent scientific tools too.

00:22:46.210 --> 00:22:50.890
They are amplifying the machine's output with Neo's willpower.

00:22:50.890 --> 00:22:52.970
It'll be difficult for the Captain to beat them.

00:22:54.560 --> 00:22:55.770
As I promised,

00:22:55.770 --> 00:23:00.980
because you gave us your Blue Water, I will spare Nadia's life.

00:23:01.610 --> 00:23:03.570
Goodbye, Nemo.

00:23:05.230 --> 00:23:08.280
I no longer have any interest in Tartessos.

00:23:09.400 --> 00:23:13.410
Shall we test the gravity bomb we just finished developing?

00:23:13.410 --> 00:23:16.910
Yes, Sir! Gravity bomb, prepare to fire!

00:23:16.910 --> 00:23:17.540
Stop it!

00:23:18.790 --> 00:23:24.420
Become a graveyard for Nemo, Old Tartessos and the Blue Noah!

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:39.350
Farewell, my dear Nemo!
